  "title": "Electric Warrior",
  "country": "UK",
  "released": "1971-09-24",
  "notes": "This is the original UK release in matt cover with lyrics printed on the rear.\nDrawn portraits on shaped standard paper inner sleeve with 'Patent No. 1,125,555' and 'HIFLY 6' printed.\nInitial copies with a free foldout poster; with or without an advertising sticker on front cover.\n\n℗ 1971\n\nB6 appears as \"Rip Off\" on cover's tracklist, but as \"Rip-Off\" in lyrics' title and on label.\n\n[cover rear:]\nRecorded at Wally Heider L.A., Media Sound N.Y., Trident and Advision Studios London\nAll songs written and composed by Marc Bolan, for Essex Music (International) Ltd\nFly Records Ltd., Dumbarton House, 68 Oxford Street, London, W1N 9LA.\nPrinted and made by the E. J. Day Group, London and Bedford.\n\n[label:]\nEssex Music Int. Ltd.\nMade in Gt Britain\n\nThere is a slightly later version [r=12840833], which separates the publishing for A3 into [l148304].\n\nRunouts are stamped, except for 'PORKY' and 'PECKO-DUCK', which are etched. ",
  "released_formatted": "24 Sep 1971",
